            <title>[LU-21337] utils: non-root lctl get_param drops last digit of stats lines</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21337</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;When a user who is not root runs "lctl get_param &amp;lt;obd&amp;gt;.*.stats", lctl&lt;br/&gt;
reads the stats over netlink.  In the plain output, the last character&lt;br/&gt;
of each counter line is lost, so the last field (sum of squares) is&lt;br/&gt;
wrong.  If that value has one digit, the field is empty.  Root (debugfs)&lt;br/&gt;
and "lctl get_param -y" print the correct value.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Same counter, read at the same moment:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;non-root plain   statfs                              309 samples [usecs] 0 26 534 267
non-root -y      statfs: {samples: 309, units: usecs, min: 0, max: 26, sum: 534, sumsquare: 2670}
root             statfs                              309 samples [usecs] 0 26 534 2670
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Cause"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Cause&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;print_out_stats() in lustre/utils/liblustreapi_param.c puts a space&lt;br/&gt;
before each field (" %s").  At YAML_MAPPING_END_EVENT it then does&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;tt&gt;buf&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;len - 1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt; = '\0'&lt;/tt&gt; to "eat last white space".  There is no&lt;br/&gt;
trailing space, so this removes the last digit of the line.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Fix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Remove the cut and print the line as it is built.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name="Reproducer"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproducer&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;$ lctl get_param -n llite.*.stats &amp;gt; /tmp/root.out        # as root
$ su &amp;lt;user&amp;gt; -c 'lctl get_param -n llite.*.stats'         # as non-root
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Compare the last field of each "samples" line between the two outputs.&lt;br/&gt;
Use a counter whose sample count does not change between the two reads.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Note: non-root netlink stats reads can also hit &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20903" title="BUG: unable to handle page fault for address: 0000000000080003. Non-root lctl get_param triggers out-of-bounds write in lustre_stats_dump() and MDS crash (2.17.0)" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20903"&gt;LU-20903&lt;/a&gt; (key table&lt;br/&gt;
overflow in lustre_stats_dump()).  The fix for this ticket is only in&lt;br/&gt;
userspace, but its test needs the &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20903" title="BUG: unable to handle page fault for address: 0000000000080003. Non-root lctl get_param triggers out-of-bounds write in lustre_stats_dump() and MDS crash (2.17.0)" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20903"&gt;LU-20903&lt;/a&gt; fix.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
